{"title":"Mock AIME 4 2006-2007 Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2006-2007_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Point\" title=\"Point\">Points</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are on the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Circumference\" title=\"Circumference\">circumference</a> of a unit <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Circle\" title=\"Circle\">circle</a> so that the measure of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/1/aa12b63f50f8f59c47be09fd2d60b8f7b9ff8153.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\widehat{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"20\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/b/24b827998def193fbf2d8ec73227dc09a0a27e63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$72^{\\circ}$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" />, the measure of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/c/28cc93fbfb5ed16e87ce30594bc806a6094fe106.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\widehat{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"20\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/d/11d0d9b28b429ef7a98b6ac8e14b6151af91ed33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36^{\\circ}$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" />, and the measure of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/1/e81c3192e927f96cd29814267058d9daae39b810.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\widehat{AC}$\" width=\"27\" height=\"19\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/3/983e30a3f86562e7b3c391929433e7d4e59bba4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$108^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"33\" height=\"13\" />. The area of the triangular shape bounded by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/c/28cc93fbfb5ed16e87ce30594bc806a6094fe106.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\widehat{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"20\" /> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Line_segment\" title=\"Line segment\">line segments</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/12517bbc31cb9026c71299b7a0d232d07e60f284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> can be written in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/a/81a57a55c6ae7038b60d65938db833c70e86c42c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{n} \\cdot \\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"43\" height=\"33\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Relatively_prime\" title=\"Relatively prime\">relatively prime</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Positive_integer\" title=\"Positive integer\">positive integers</a>. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/b/53bf1afcb274a3bb84338109fffec8a1f1c02008.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m + n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2006-2007_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2007_4_MockAIME-4.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/de/2007_4_MockAIME-4.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"340\" height=\"353\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p><p>Let the center of the circle be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.  The area of the desired region is easily seen to be that of sector <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/d/76d9b534de592b2a7fc63b97e1f0faab799204e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BOC$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> plus the area of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/9/cd97737c9a1eb5146725902d4e4c4bda1388129b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AOB$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> minus the area of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/2/0129518bfc1d0df50eeb37d3d6a62b0a0327a85e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AOC$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />.  Using the area formula <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/4/7e4dd843e4b1eeab4a69698523f8dcd03bd405ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K_{\\triangle XYZ} = \\frac{1}{2} XY \\cdot YZ \\cdot \\sin Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"222\" height=\"37\" /> to compute the areas of the two triangles, this is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/e/c2eb83ee1cdc00e844c5764da264337d3976c7e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi \\cdot \\frac{36}{360} + \\frac{1}{2}\\sin 72^\\circ - \\frac{1}{2}\\sin108^{\\circ} = \\frac{1}{10}\\cdot \\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"313\" height=\"38\" />, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/a/72a6ee4f577ba351c7285c1297e657f20e340190.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + 10 = 011$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"99\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2006-2007_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2006-2007\" title=\"Mock AIME 4 2006-2007\">Mock AIME 4 2006-2007</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2006-2007_Problems\" title=\"Mock AIME 4 2006-2007 Problems\">Problems</a></b>, <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/viewtopic.php?t=125025\">Source</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2006-2007_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"Mock AIME 4 2006-2007 Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2006-2007_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"Mock AIME 4 2006-2007 Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2006-2007_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"Mock AIME 4 2006-2007 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2006-2007_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"Mock AIME 4 2006-2007 Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2006-2007_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"Mock AIME 4 2006-2007 Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2006-2007_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"Mock AIME 4 2006-2007 Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2006-2007_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"Mock AIME 4 2006-2007 Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2006-2007_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"Mock AIME 4 2006-2007 Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2006-2007_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"Mock AIME 4 2006-2007 Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2006-2007_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"Mock AIME 4 2006-2007 Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2006-2007_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"Mock AIME 4 2006-2007 Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2006-2007_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"Mock AIME 4 2006-2007 Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2006-2007_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"Mock AIME 4 2006-2007 Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2006-2007_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"Mock AIME 4 2006-2007 Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2006-2007_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"Mock AIME 4 2006-2007 Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2006-2007_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"Mock AIME 4 2006-2007 Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nN